### AEROSPACE RESEARCH & DEMONSTRATION NOTICE

1. **Competition & Research Context**:
   This software was engineered as an autonomous spaceflight physiological monitoring, mathematical sentry, and clinical AI voice advisory demonstrator for the **NASA International Space Apps Challenge 2026**.

2. **Non-Clinical / Research Prototype Disclaimer**:
   H.E.L.I.O.S is a technological prototype and engineering proof-of-concept designed to illustrate offline autonomous medical decision-support during deep-space communication latency (e.g., Earth-Mars transit). This software is NOT certified as a medical device by the United States Food and Drug Administration (FDA), European Medicines Agency (EMA), or any equivalent regulatory body. It is not intended to replace certified medical practitioners, flight surgeons, or certified ground-support clinical protocols.

3. **Data Attribution**:
   Physiological baselines, assay reference distributions, and biomarker metrics are derived from publicly accessible open science datasets provided by the **NASA Open Science Data Repository (OSDR)** (including OSD-575 and OSD-569 from the SpaceX Inspiration4 SOMA spaceflight research collection) and published spaceflight physiology literature.
